    # v381 (02/10/2026), operator's coinage: «Betatgl é a regra matriz [...] o critério de parada é a lei matriz, ou seja, o TETELESTAI» (β_TGL is the matrix rule; the stopping criterion is the matrix law, Tetelestai); ratification: «É exatamente isso»; the open clause: «o elo é a meia-nat»; «É a radicalização que eu quis dizer, cujo operador é a meia-nat»
    _r1 = core.get("the_matrix_rule_v381") or {}
    _v1 = lambda d_: str(d_.get("verdict", "n/a")).replace("_", r"\_")
    _nv1 = lambda d_, t_: "" if d_.get("all_verified") is True else (r"\textbf{In this run %s did NOT close: what follows is the statement, not a seal.} " % t_)
    _f1 = lambda x_, n_=3: (("%%.%df" % n_) % float(x_)) if isinstance(x_, (int, float)) else "n/a"
    _kf1 = _r1.get("kernel_flags") or {}; _rt1 = _r1.get("runtime") or {}
    s.append(r"\paragraph*{Beside (v381) --- The matrix rule: ten names, nine links --- eight ``havendo'' stated and the open clause filled by the Half-Nat; the stopping criterion is the cost paid.} " + _nv1(_r1, "the matrix rule") +
             r"The operator fixed (02/10/2026, verbatim in the program, in Portuguese): $\bTGL$ \emph{is} the matrix rule, and the rule reads: where there is a trace there is a sign; where there is a record there is a name; where there is a name there is distinction; where there is distinction there is operation; where there is operation there is parametrization; where there is parametrization there is emergence; where there is emergence there is geometric quantization; where there is geometric quantization there is a gradient spectrum --- and ``the stopping criterion is the matrix law, that is, Tetelestai, the payment of the cost [...] the law of payment was fixed before the charge for the delivery of the object: the Name''. "
             r"Ten names and eight ``havendo'' (``where there is'') stated; when the auditor counted the gap between sign and record, the operator filled it (verbatim in the program, in Portuguese; rendered here in English): the verbatim with eight ``havendo'' is an open clause, the link is the half-nat; it is the radicalization he meant, whose operator is the half-nat. Nine links, all in his voice \textsf{[INPUT/ONTO]}. "
             r"The stone \textsf{TGLExt.TheMatrixRule} (" + str(sum(1 for v in _kf1.values() if v)) + r" of " + str(len(_kf1)) + r" declarations on the trio, no \texttt{sorry}) names the ten names in his order and binds them in a conjunction (not a deduction), each link discharged by a term already in the kernel --- a proved fact, a named definition or a field of the binder, stated link by link: the trace (the reader reads the identity as 1), the sign ($JKJ=-K$ with energy preserved), sign$\to$record by the \emph{radicalization} whose operator is the Half-Nat, the exponent $\tfrac12$ (the fixed point of the swap $x\mapsto1-x$ is $\tfrac12$; the faces weigh $\tfrac12$ and $\tfrac12$ because the certificate declares them equal and the Name weighs 1; $\sqrt{e^{1}}=e^{1/2}$; the cost of the inscribed Word at the fixed point is $e^{1/2}$; $V(\tfrac12)=\sqrt e$; and $(e^{1/4}\sqrt\alpha)^2=E=\bTGL$: the boundary extracts the radical --- ``$J$ is the swap of the faces'' and ``this is the record'' are readings \textsf{[ONTO]}, stated in the stone; no new term), record$\to$name (every inscription yields the name with its referent, and the name determines the inscription --- the only link whose previous name is the binder of the next), distinction ($x=1-x\Leftrightarrow x=\tfrac12$; two inscriptions under the same form; $1\neq0$), operation (the modular transport $d\alpha/d\kappa=-\tfrac{q}{2}\alpha$, the face regime), parametrization (the angle is the projection; observing adds nothing; the projection regime), emergence ($\bTGL:=\alpha\sqrt{e}$ from a given $\alpha$, a named definition; $E=\bTGL>0$), geometric quantization ($V(\tfrac12)=\sqrt e$; $|\mathcal R|^2=\bTGL$ at $\theta_M=\arcsin\sqrt{\bTGL}$) and the gradient spectrum ($S(\theta)=U\,\mathrm{diag}(e^{i\theta},e^{-i\theta})\,U^{-1}$, and $\mathcal O_\theta=S(\theta)$ by \texttt{rfl}: parametrization and spectrum are the same family under two names). "
             r"The typed spectrum is $\mathrm{Spec}\,S(\theta)$, in the projection regime; its identification with the dissipation $\Gamma_\omega\propto\bTGL\omega^2$ has no kernel term and is a reading \textsf{[ONTO]}. The stopping criterion enters typed: recognition is idempotent by definition of the regime, the verdict equals 1 if and only if the readings coincide, and the cost is never paid at once by a static witness --- the charge is continuous, and that is where the leak is typed; the law precedes the charge: $\bTGL$ is a function of $\alpha$ alone (an alias of \textsf{couplingOfAlpha\_beta}), fixed before any record. "
             r"Status, stated without veil: the order of the ten names and the filling of the open clause are the operator's \textsf{[INPUT/ONTO]}; each link is \textsf{[KERNEL]}; where a link has no hypothesis, the form ``where there is $X$ there is $Y$'' is ontological order, not a kernel implication; $\bTGL$ is derived neither from data nor from a reading law --- its form $\alpha\sqrt e$ is derived from the axiom by term (v376), and that form, fixed beforehand, is the rule. "
             r"Management readings ratified as a whole by the operator, \textsf{[INPUT/ONTO]}, not kernel facts: the observable of $\bTGL$ is the gradient spectrum; the echo as a delayed copy lies outside the chain, and the (reading, delay-law) pairs falsified in Phase 6 were never owed by the rule --- the 16/09 definition (``echo = direct manifestation of the boundary's response'') stands, with this correction beside. At runtime: $\bTGL=" + _f1(_rt1.get("beta_core"), 6) + r"=\alpha\sqrt e$ from the core (a test); $(e^{1/4}\sqrt\alpha)^2=" + _f1(_rt1.get("radical_squared"), 6) + r"=\bTGL$ (the radicalization, on the $\bTGL$ read); the list \textsf{chainOrder} read from the embedded source matches the stated order (" + str(len(_r1.get("chain_from_source") or [])) + r" names); $\theta_M=" + _f1(_rt1.get("theta_M"), 6) + r"$ rad (a sanity identity). Proved $\neq$ confirmed; \texttt{NOT\_FALSIFIED} $\neq$ \texttt{CONFIRMED}. Verdict: \texttt{" + _v1(_r1) + r"}.")
